        {
          "type": "paragraph",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "value": "The spiral treatise argues that time does not move in a straight line or a simple circle, but in a spiral: it revisits similar patterns while moving forward, so nothing repeats exactly. Each moment is both new and tied to the past; change happens through repetition, not in spite of it."
            }
          ]
